Leave wl_array_release's data pointer as the firmware's Wayland 1.11 does.

QtWayland 5.4's input-context plugin (webOS 4) destroys its wl_registry after
QWaylandDisplay has called wl_display_disconnect. proxy_destroy then writes into
the released object map: harmless with 1.11, whose release only frees the data,
but a write through WL_ARRAY_POISON_PTR (address 4 + 4 * id) since then, which
crashed qml-runner at every exit.

--- a/src/wayland-util.c
+++ b/src/wayland-util.c
@@ -103,7 +103,6 @@
 wl_array_release(struct wl_array *array)
 {
 	free(array->data);
-	array->data = WL_ARRAY_POISON_PTR;
 }
 
 WL_EXPORT void *
